    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19816" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεργαΐζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>romance</i>, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βέργη</span>
			: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βεργαῖος</span></b> 
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕθλος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
				</span></i>
			 in Gloss. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Oxy.</u>
				1801.50
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">β. διήγημα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Str.
					2.3.5
				</span></i>
			 (Antiphanes of Berga in Thrace was proverbial for his 'tall'
			stories).</div>
